$ yubikey-backup.sh restore --key backup.key --passin pass:test-only bk/yubikey-db.cms.0
The backup, made <TIMESTAMP> UTC: 3 YubiKeys (of 3 users), 1 service account, 1 group.
The database <T>_db now: 4 YubiKeys (of 4 users), 1 service account, 1 group.
The restore puts the backup's tables back, and so undoes what changed since:
  YubiKeys added since the backup, which go: carol vvccccdddddd
  YubiKeys changed since the backup, which are put back as they were: test.user2 cbdefghijklr (enabled again)
  Service accounts changed since the backup, which are put back as they were: svc.backup (its password)
  Groups added since the backup, which go: helpdesk
  Groups deleted since the backup, which come back: netadmins
Counters that are ahead now stay, and so do the anycast checks' keys.
yubikey-backup.sh: error: restore: answer on a terminal, or add --yes
[exit 3]

